<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F5.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 5</span>: </span><span id="A4.F5.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Absolute results of weak accuracy, strong accuracy, and quality versus the height of the ontology tree with multiple hypotheses under zero-shot (<span id="A4.F5.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">top</span>), 8-shot in-distribution (<span id="A4.F5.8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">middle</span>), and 8-shot out-of-distribution (<span id="A4.F5.8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">bottom</span>).</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>LLM example responses</h2>

<section id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"><em id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Self-verification</em></h5>

<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">World Model:</span> Amy is a dalpist. Pamela is a dalpist. Jerry is a dalpist.

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Observations:</span> Amy is rainy. Jerry is rainy. Pamela is rainy.

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hypotheses:</span> Dalpists are rainy.

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LLM Output:</span> <span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;think&gt;</span> … Suppose Dalpists are rainy. Since Amy and Jerry and Pamela are dalpists, they are all rainy. This hypothesis can explain all observations. <span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;/think&gt;</span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"><em id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Wrong ontology direction</em></h5>

<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">World Model:</span> Porpors are dalpists. Nicole is a gergit. Sarpers are dalpists. Every gergit is a dalpist. Debra is a dalpist. Each dalpist is rainy. Every porpor is not cold. Raymond is a gergit. Each porpor is translucent. Amy is a porpor. Jerry is a dalpist. Pamela is a dalpist. Sharon is a gergit. Edward is a dalpist. Michael is a sarper.

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Observations:</span> Sharon is moderate. Barbara is not cold. Debra is liquid. Barbara is rainy. Barbara is liquid. Barbara is translucent. Amy is a rompus. Raymond is moderate. Jerry is a rompus. Edward is liquid. Pamela is a rompus. Nicole is moderate.

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ground truth hypotheses:</span> Dalpists are rompuses. Every dalpist is liquid. Each gergit is moderate. Barbara is a porpor.

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LLM Output:</span> … Rompuses are dalpists. …</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"><em id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Ignore the ontology and produce unnecessary hypotheses</em></h5>

<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">World Model:</span> David is a sorple. Each sorple is a dropant. Each hilper is a thorpin. Rimpees are scrompists. Brian is a sorple. Dropants are gompers. Angela is a gomper. Each thorpin is a gomper. Every scrompist is a gomper.

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Observations:</span> David is rainy. Brian is rainy. Angela is rainy.

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ground truth hypotheses:</span> Every gomper is rainy.

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LLM Output:</span> … Every gomper is rainy. Every dropant is rainy. …</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"><em id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Fall back to rival hypothesee</em></h5>

<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">World Model:</span> Rorpants are dolpers. Every worple is a wumpus. Each drompee is moderate. Ashley is a rorpant. Fimples are dolpers. Ronald is a wumpus. Wumpuses are gwompants. Yompins are dolpers. Brian is a dolper. Michelle is a worple. Each dolper is a gwompant. Shirley is a rorpant. Sandra is a bempin. Linda is a fimple. Drompees are pale. Jack is a yompin. Each drompee is a bempin. Bempins are cold. Bempins are gwompants. Emma is a gwompant. Michael is a gwompant.

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Observations:</span> Shirley is a borpin. Christopher is pale. Emma is a borpin. Brian is salty. Michael is salty. Christopher is a borpin. Christopher is cold. Ashley is salty. Christopher is moderate.

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ground truth hypotheses:</span> Each gwompant is a borpin. Each gwompant is salty. Christopher is a drompee.

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LLM Output:</span> … Shirley is a borpin. …</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"><em id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px5.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Hallucinated entities</em></h5>

<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">World Model:</span> Jonathan is a rifpist. Yimples are dull. Samantha is a rifpist. Karen is a gwompant. Scott is a jelgit. Olivia is a frompor. Maria is a lirpin. Twimpees are lirpins. Each rifpist is aggressive. Frompors are jelgits. Jessica is a jelgit. Amanda is a twimpee. Rifpists are jelgits. Each lirpin is a jelgit. Yimples are small. Each gwompant is a frompor. Each yimple is a rifpist.

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Observations:</span> Mary is not overcast. Scott is not overcast. Jonathan is not overcast. Samantha is a kurpor. Mary is aggressive. Jessica is a kurpor. Olivia is a kurpor. Mary is small. Mary is dull.

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ground truth hypotheses:</span> Every jelgit is a kurpor. Jelgits are not overcast. Mary is a yimple.

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LLM Output:</span> … Mary is a dolphant. …</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"><em id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px6.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Confuse members with concepts</em></h5>

<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">World Model:</span> Delpees are impuses. Yumpuses are delpees. Rebecca is an impus. Kathleen is a rifpist. Each impus is rainy. Thomas is a delpee. Lompees are arpers. Each bempin is an impus. Stephen is a bempin. Every impus is shy. Laura is a yumpus. Every arper is an impus. Stephanie is an arper. Lompees are moderate. Rifpists are bempins.

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Observations:</span> Frank is moderate. Frank is rainy. Frank is shy.

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ground truth hypotheses:</span> Frank is a lompee.

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LLM Output:</span> … Lompee is Frank. …</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
